# Authority and Canonical Sources

This compact representation owns two distinct dossier concerns for
{{PROJECT_NAME}}: interpretation/precedence and concern-to-source routing. It
does not create permission. The conceptual artifact IDs remain `DOS-0002` and
`DOS-0003`; they share this file because their owner, authority, lifecycle,
review cadence, sensitivity, and retention are aligned.

## Authority and precedence (`DOS-0002`)

1. Current user, platform, tool, contractual, and legal constraints.
2. Applicable repository instructions.
3. Live project policy and accepted project-specific decisions.
4. Executable or operational evidence for current-state claims.
5. Canonical dossier material for intended state.
6. Current-state and conformance records.
7. Plans, registers, and handoff views.
8. Provenance, historical material, and generated reports.

Current behavior does not become the intended target merely because it exists.
Target documentation does not prove implementation. Unresolved conflicts must
be recorded as findings or open questions.

## Canonical source routing (`DOS-0003`)

| Concern | Minimal edit source | Standard/High-Assurance edit source | Other representations |
|---|---|---|---|
| Artifact metadata and applicability | `machine-readable/artifact-registry.json` | same | `ARTIFACT_CATALOG.json` and `machine-readable/path-authority.json` are generated mirrors |
| Project definition | `canonical/executive-project-definition.md` | same | summaries link here |
| Requirement explanation and vocabulary | `canonical/requirements-and-constraints.md` | same | never independently duplicated |
| Individual requirement records | `canonical/requirements-and-constraints.md` | `machine-readable/requirements.json` | Markdown explains and summarizes |
| Architecture or outcome model | `canonical/architecture-or-outcome-model.md` | same, plus declared specialist model sources | generated diagrams name their source |
| Decision questions, recommendations, selections, reviews, and closure sequence | `.agent/decisions/governance-register.json` | same | Markdown workbook and trade-off report templates are human review projections |
| Durable accepted decisions | `.agent/decisions/DEC-####*.md` | same | a `DREG-####` entry links accepted authority but cannot replace it |
| Constraints and gate explanation | `canonical/constraints-gates-and-readiness.md` | same | gate records remain proposed until adopted |
| Individual gate records | `validation/QUALITY_GATES.json` | same | project-maintained, not generated evidence |
| Current observed state | `current-state/README.md` after direct inspection | same or a registry-declared observation store | scaffold text is `not_assessed`, not an observation |
| Individual conformance findings | `conformance/README.md` | `machine-readable/findings.json` | Markdown owns method and summary |
| Individual plan items | `plans/README.md` | `machine-readable/plan.json` | Markdown owns method and summary |
| RAIDQ items | `registers/README.md` | `machine-readable/raidq.json` | Markdown owns vocabulary and summary |
| Source records | `provenance/README.md` | `machine-readable/sources.json` | Markdown owns method and summary |
| Evidence metadata | `validation/README.md` | `machine-readable/evidence-index.json` | executed reports are immutable evidence |
| Dossier version and supersession | `VERSION.md`; `SUPERSESSION.json` | same | `history/` is noncurrent |
| Handoff | `handoff/START_HERE.md` | same | navigation only; mutable facts stay in their owners |
| Integrity | explicit refresh command | same | integrity outputs are generated evidence |

`machine-readable/artifact-registry.json` is the project-local edit source for
artifact types, physical representations, applicability, owners, review state,
and source direction. Generated, historical, proposed, or handoff material
must not silently replace an edit source.

The decision-governance register owns tracking and review only. Accepted
`DEC-####` records own durable decision authority. A recommendation or owner
selection cannot be promoted by a handoff, template, or structural validator.

Separation is required if the two concerns later diverge in ownership,
lifecycle, review, authority, sensitivity, or retention. That change requires
an explicit registry migration and must retain stable conceptual IDs.
